        "original_id": "ac10a41a-5c62-55ad-8793-62a24ccbe5dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacky Ickx, Pedro Rodríguez\n- Organizations: BRM, Ferrari\n- Events: 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, 1979 Can-Am season, 24 Hours of Le Mans, Dakar Rally\n- Topics: Formula One, Can-Am Championship\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, Pedro Rodríguez finished second for BRM.\n- In the 1968 Belgian Grand Prix, Ferrari driver Jacky Ickx finished third.\n- Jacky Ickx was born on 1 January 1945 in Brussels and is a Belgian former racing driver.\n- Jacky Ickx won the 24 Hours of Le Mans six times.\n- Jacky Ickx achieved eight wins and 25 podium finishes in Formula One.\n- In 1979, Jacky Ickx won the Can-Am Championship after winning five of the ten rounds and finishing second at Road Atlanta.\n- Jacky Ickx was also a former winner of the Dakar Rally.",
